<LegalPage title="Terms of Use" description="Terms for using the Destiny Global Opportunities website and the consultancy services of Destiny Global Solutions Limited." updated="22 November 2026" draft={false}>
  <p>These terms apply to your use of the {site.platformName} website (destinyglobals.com), operated by <strong>{site.companyName}</strong>, a company registered in {site.registration.jurisdiction} under number {site.registration.number}, registered office {site.registration.registeredOffice}. By using the website you accept these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the website.</p>

  <h2>1. What this website offers</h2>
  <p>The website provides free information about scholarships, fellowships, PhD and research positions, conferences, universities, visas and studying abroad, together with free tools and guides. It also describes the optional consultancy services we offer.</p>

  <h2>2. Information only — not advice</h2>
  <p>Content on this website is general information. It is not legal, immigration, financial or professional advice for your situation. Opportunity details are summaries of official sources and can change at any time, so always confirm on the official source before you act. See our <a href={url('/disclaimer/')}>Disclaimer</a> and <a href={url('/scholarship-verification/')}>how we verify</a>.</p>

  <h2>3. Free tools are estimates</h2>
  <p>The eligibility checker, grade converter, ECTS calculator, visa money calculator, application planner and checklists give estimates and reminders based on published rules. Universities, scholarship providers and governments make their own assessments and may reach a different result. Do not rely on a tool’s result alone when making a decision or submitting an application.</p>

  <h2>4. No guarantees</h2>
  <p>We do not guarantee admission, scholarship selection, visa approval, funding or any other outcome. Those decisions are made only by the relevant institutions, providers and authorities.</p>

  <h2>5. Applying directly is always free</h2>
  <p>You can always apply directly through the official website of a scholarship or university. Our consultancy assistance is a separate, optional service. Using the website does not create any client relationship with us.</p>

  <h2>6. Consultancy services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Agreement first.</strong> Before any paid work starts, we confirm in writing (by email or WhatsApp) what the service includes, the fee, how and when it is paid, and the expected timing. That written confirmation, together with these terms, forms our agreement.</li>
    <li><strong>Fees and refunds.</strong> Fees and any refund conditions are those stated in that written confirmation. Fees paid to us are for our assistance only — they never include application fees, visa fees or other charges paid to official bodies, which you pay directly to them.</li>
    <li><strong>Your responsibilities.</strong> You are responsible for giving us true, complete and genuine information and documents, for checking everything before it is submitted, for meeting deadlines, and for submitting applications that must be submitted by you personally.</li>
    <li><strong>Honesty.</strong> We will not prepare, alter or submit false or misleading documents or information. We may end a service immediately if we are asked to do so.</li>
    <li><strong>Who we are not.</strong> We are not a law firm, and we are not a government-authorised immigration adviser or representative. We do not represent you before any authority. Where your case needs regulated legal or immigration advice, we will tell you to seek a qualified, authorised professional.</li>
    <li><strong>Cancellation.</strong> You can cancel a service by telling us in writing. If you are a consumer, you also keep any cancellation rights the law gives you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. External websites</h2>
  <p>We link to official third-party websites and platforms for your convenience. We do not control them and are not responsible for their content, availability, fees or processes.</p>

  <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not misuse the website: do not try to disrupt or hack it, upload harmful code, scrape or copy substantial parts of it for commercial use or redistribution without our written permission, or use it for anything unlawful or fraudulent.</p>

  <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>The website design, original text, tools, illustrations and logo belong to {site.companyName} unless stated otherwise. You may share links and use the content for your own personal, non-commercial study planning. Names and logos of scholarship programmes, universities and organisations belong to their owners and are used only to identify the opportunities described.</p>

  <h2>10. Availability</h2>
  <p>We provide the website free of charge and “as is”. We try to keep it available and accurate but cannot promise it will always be available, error-free or up to date.</p>

  <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss arising from your use of, or reliance on, the website or its free tools, including missed deadlines, rejected applications or decisions made by third parties. For paid services, our total liability is limited to the fees you paid us for that service. Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or any other liability that cannot be limited by law, and nothing affects your statutory rights as a consumer.</p>

  <h2>12. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows the latest version. Continuing to use the website after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have jurisdiction. If you are a consumer living elsewhere, you keep the protection of the mandatory laws of your country.</p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>
